On main: a config Old|New on a tree with Old/a.txt -> after apply_changes the tree holds New/ and an empty Old/. The files move, the directory does not: _collect_dir only records files, apply_changes creates the new parent and removes the old file, never the old directory. An empty directory whose name matches a rule is not renamed at all (no change is recorded for it).
Work: after apply, a renamed directory is gone from its old place (remove the old directories that the apply emptied, deepest first - never a directory that still holds something), and decide with a test what an empty matching directory does (rename it, recorded as a change and shown in the diff as a rename). Tests on a temp tree.

